            <ArticleTitle>Stent deformity caused by coronary artery spasm.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>800-1</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Previous studies have shown that coronary stents have radial strength above the pressure induced by coronary artery spasm. This case report describes a stent deformity caused by coronary artery spasm during percutaneous coronary intervention.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
